{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>I would scatter them.</b> Some say these are three words, but the correct view is that it has no complement, and its meaning is like 'I would destroy them,' because after it comes 'I would make the memory of them cease from men,' and so all of them would die. And were it as the grammarians hold, that the meaning is 'I would scatter them in every direction,' the meaning would not cohere. And some say 'I would devastate them in my nostril' [i.e., in my anger], and its meaning is 'I would annihilate them,' like 'I would make them cease,' and the meaning would come doubled, and this would be correct were it not for the alef of אפיהם, for it ought to be אנפיהם, and the meaning 'I would be angry with them.' But the first is correct." "The meaning of <b>I said</b> is, in human language: I said in my heart."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:26:05.925118909Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}